WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.640 --> 00:00:05.370
- And you see, string theory
is a multiverse theory.

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:08.200
So people say, first of all,
"What is string theory?"

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:10.500
String theory simply says
that all the particles

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:13.570
we see in nature, the
electron, the proton, quarks,

00:00:13.570 --> 00:00:16.110
what have you, are nothing but vibrations

00:00:16.110 --> 00:00:18.080
on a musical string,

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:19.813
on a tiny, tiny little string.

00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:22.240
You know, J. Robert Oppenheimer,

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:24.470
the creator of the atomic bomb,

00:00:24.470 --> 00:00:26.860
was so frustrated in the 1950s

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:30.020
with all these subatomic
particles being created

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:32.920
in our atom smashers, that he announced.

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:36.220
He announced one day, that the Nobel Prize

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:38.800
in physics should go to the physicist

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:43.110
who does not discover a
new particle that year.

00:00:43.110 --> 00:00:45.420
Well today, we think they're
nothing but musical notes

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:47.780
on these tiny little vibrating strings.

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:49.580
So, what is physics?

00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:51.660
Physics is the harmonies you can write

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:53.450
on vibrating strings.

00:00:53.450 --> 00:00:54.980
What is chemistry?

00:00:54.980 --> 00:00:59.700
Chemistry is the melodies you
can play on these strings.

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:01.013
What is the universe?

00:01:01.900 --> 00:01:05.100
The universe is a symphony of strings.

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:08.030
And then, what is the mind of God,

00:01:08.030 --> 00:01:10.540
that Albert Einstein so
eloquently wrote about

00:01:10.540 --> 00:01:13.240
for the last 30 years of his life?

00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:14.410
The mind of God

00:01:15.250 --> 00:01:17.600
would be cosmic music,

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:20.793
resonating through
11-dimensional hyperspace.

